course: dictionary
lesson: 6833
title: Outcrop: rock that sticks out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An outcrop is a part of rock that sticks out of the ground or a hillside, so you can see it from far away. The word «rocky» in «rocky outcrops» is a clue: it tells you the outcrops are made of rock.
explain: «Serengeti lions rest on rocky outcrops called kopjes, which give them shade, a lookout and safe dens for cubs.» The lions climb up high, so an outcrop must be a raised place. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Outcrop has a second meaning too. A small group of something appearing in an unexpected place can be called an outcrop. In a city, an outcrop of shops is a small cluster of shops in a place you did not expect to find them.
fact: An outcrop is a part of rock that sticks out of the ground or a hillside.
fact: «Outcrop» can also mean a small group of something appearing in an unexpected place.
fact: «Serengeti lions rest on rocky outcrops called kopjes»: these rocks give the lions shade, a lookout and safe dens for cubs.
fact: Geologists study rock outcrops to see layers of rock and fossils.
fact: On a walk, outcrops are good places to look at different kinds of rock, such as granite and limestone.
exercise: «Serengeti lions rest on rocky outcrops called kopjes.» What is an outcrop? | A tall tree on the plain | A deep hole dug by animals | A wide, flat river | *A part of rock that sticks out of the ground or a hillside
exercise: Why do geologists study rock outcrops? | To make the ground softer | *To see layers of rock and fossils | To count how many lions live nearby | To find the best place to buy food
exercise: In a city, Mia sees «an outcrop of shops» behind the station. What does outcrop mean here? | *A small cluster of shops in an unexpected place | A large field of grass | A bus stop with a roof | A road that goes uphill
test: On a walk, which two kinds of rock might you look at on an outcrop? | Sand and water | *Granite and limestone | Ice and snow | Wood and paper
test: «Serengeti lions rest on rocky outcrops called kopjes.» Why do the lions use these rocks? | To grow tall trees | To hide from the rain only | *For shade, a lookout and safe dens for cubs | To keep the sea away
exam: Which sentence uses outcrop to mean a part of rock sticking out of a hillside? | The outcrop of shops opened early on Saturday | *The grey outcrop stood out above the green grass of the hill | The outcrop of noise came from the school hall | The outcrop of children waited at the bus stop
